\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.6}{\ignorespaces ULD compares ranked probability mass after temperature scaling, sorting, and zero-padding to a common vocabulary length \cite {boizard2024towardscrosstokenizerdistillation}.\relax }}{9}{figure.caption.10}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.7}{\ignorespaces Example of sparse routing and expert specialization in a mixture-of-experts architecture \cite {wikimedia_deepseek_moe_mla_image,deepseekai2024deepseekv2strongeconomicalefficient}. Although our setting is multi-teacher distillation rather than token-level MoE language modeling, the same principles of learned routing, sparse activation, and load balancing are directly relevant.\relax }}{11}{figure.caption.11}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.8}{\ignorespaces Illustration of gradient alignment in pooled logit-gradient space. The learned gate first proposes constrained routing weights \(\hat {p}_i^{(b)}\); gradient alignment then activates only sufficiently aligned teachers. If none are active, the router falls back to the least-negative teacher.\relax }}{13}{figure.caption.12}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.9}{\ignorespaces A high CKA score is not sufficient to conclude that layer-wise transfer will remove the downstream performance gap. Representation similarity and task performance are related but not equivalent.\relax }}{15}{figure.caption.13}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.1}{\ignorespaces Overview of the current method. A student-side deep gate proposes sparse teacher weights, top-\(k\) and capacity constraints determine routed teachers, a balancing loss regularizes teacher usage, and cosine alignment filters the routed teachers before KD aggregation. Sample superscripts are omitted when clear.\relax }}{17}{figure.caption.14}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.2}{\ignorespaces Gate architecture used in the current implementation. The router pools student hidden states over supervised positions, applies LayerNorm, uses a gated MLP block \(\mathrm {SiLU}(\mathbf {g}) \odot \mathbf {v}\), and outputs one routing logit per teacher.\relax }}{19}{figure.caption.15}%
